        "description": "<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"\" data-caption=\"\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: The Verge\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/03/STK414_AI_CVIRGINIA_I__0001_11.png?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\t\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"has-text-align-none\">First came the AI beauty pageant. Then the AI music contests. Now, there is an award for AI Personality of the Year - perhaps the inevitable next step for the AI influencer economy as it transforms from quirky novelty into a serious and lucrative industry. </p>\n<p class=\"has-text-align-none\">The contest, a joint venture between generative AI studio OpenArt and AI-powered creator platform Fanvue, with backing from AI voice company ElevenLabs, opens on Monday and runs for a month. The organizers said it is intended to \"celebrate the creative talent 'behind' AI Influencers\" and recognize their growing commercial and cultural clout. </p>\n<p class=\"has-text",
